          "transliteration": "pṛthivyai cainamagneśca daivī vāgāviśati | sā vai daivī vāgyayā yadyadeva vadati tattadbhavati ||",
          "translation": "From the earth and from fire, divine speech enters into him. And verily that is divine speech whereby, whatever he says, comes to be.",
