          "transliteration": "atha rūpāṇāṃ cakṣurityetadeṣāmukthamato hi sarvāṇi rūpāṇyuttiṣṭhanti | etadeṣām̐ sāmaitaddhi sarvai rūpaiḥ samam | etadeṣāṃ brahmaitaddhi sarvāṇi rūpāṇi bibharti ||",
          "translation": "Next, of the forms, that which is called Eye is the Uktha (hymn), for from it all forms arise. It is their Sâman (song), for it is the same as all forms. It is their Brahman (prayer), for it supports all forms.",
